<title>CHILE: Chile's Escondida details July copper output.</title>
<headline>Chile's Escondida details July copper output.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's Minera Escondida Ltda said on Monday it had produced 63,233 tonnes of copper in July and a total of 543,581 tonnes in the first seven months of 1997.</p>
<p>Escondida, which last year passed Codelco's Chuquicamata mine as the world's largest copper pit last year, is owned by Australia's Broken Hill Proprietary and RTZ Corp plc.</p>
<p>The following are production figures for Escondida</p>
<p>				 July		   Jan-July Copper concentrates</p>
<p>58,012 tonnes N/A Copper cathodes 5,221 N/A</p>
<p> TOTAL			63,233 tonnes	 543,581 tonnes Gold concentrates</p>
<p>12,992 ounces 106,687 ounces</p>
<p>((--Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211))</p>
</text>
